WEBVTT

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.600
Major.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.830
Hey, Major!

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.980
What was that? Virtual reality?

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.460
I'm on vacation.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.720
Would you mind not entering my cyber lobby so casually?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.470
My condolences.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.530
There's been a terrorist bombing in Nishinouchi.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.120
The vics were an executive at a foreign-owned water company,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.430
a Trade Ministry official, and a 
domestic weapons manufacturer.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.400
The top-priority entry in the terrorism prediction list you gave Public Security was right on the money.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.000
I assume they were in a secret 
meeting to settle on water prices.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.360
Everything's in smithereens, 
including some Foreign Affairs guards.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.480
There was also an explosion at 
the Yamanote dam, by the way.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.330
The dam?

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.820
Dunno if it's related.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:32.990
But it essentially belongs to a foreign-owned water 
company, and there's a retired Trade official on staff.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.970
The bureaucrats' turf wars are intense in that industry.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.140
So, who asked for us?

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.100
Section 9, as usual.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.830
They failed to put your list to good use,
 but they did track the perps.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.940
They say they can't secure 'em, though. Too outgunned.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.640
Call everyone in. I'm coming too.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.370
Work calls?

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.010
I'm sorry.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.290
Five hours, seven minutes.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.500
That's a record-length vacation for you.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.610
Are you consulting for the police today?

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.670
Or the Cyberbrain Development Bureau?

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.560
I'll make it up to you.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.430
Don't forget what we talked about.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.710
Are you serious?

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.560
Of course.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.090
You should get going.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.340
Your customers are never exactly patient, are they now?

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.020
Yes.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:37.710
Wow, you've been with that guy for three months!

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.570
That's a new record.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.680
Would you mind not using that 
Ghost infiltration key so casually?

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:59.070
Your precinct ID'd him as Detective Mizuki Naoharu.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.530
Is that right?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.450
Yeah. He's my senior.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.370
Is this all he had on him?

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.330
His holster was empty.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.790
His piece must've been washed away or stolen.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.710
It's hard to believe the gun under 
his jacket would get washed away.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.100
And it'd be odd for someone to 
steal his gun but leave his wallet.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.960
A prosthetics specialist...

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.230
He sure doesn't look cyberized.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.820
Lieutenant, your guys rounded up all the unclaimed property in the area, right?

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.360
Let's look for something else that ties back to him.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.290
You want me to be your errand boy?

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.940
If the dam incident was really an accident, yes.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:48.950
Lieutenant!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.580
I found something odd.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.560
What are these?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.000
They look like prosthetics, but...

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.030
Mermaid's Legs...

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:17.770
Report.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.320
Lots of injured cops.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.230
Six perps still going strong.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.200
They're on their way to Ward 4.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.700
They see right through the police strategy.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.910
They secured an escape route ahead of time.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.370
This group is highly trained.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.740
Their commander must be somewhere out there.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.330
Ishikawa!

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:40.830
I picked up their line!

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.130
The seventh one. This is their leader.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.190
This is a cutting-edge ghost lock.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.630
Don't waste time resisting.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.670
I'll make him order his friends to surrender.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.630
Ishikawa, run a forced recognition program.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:30.550
Roger.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:32.970
Abort the operation.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.060
Throw down your guns and surrender.

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:40.360
Repeat: abort the operation and surrender.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:44.480
Huh?

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.150
Aw, no shootout?

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:54.120
I captured one!

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.090
Hey, you're pretty useful!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.960
We got the last one.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.470
Good. Hand them all over to Public Security.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.550
A virus alert?

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:12.800
It's the man you captured!

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.320
<i>This pain...</i>

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.950
<i>The ghost lock released?</i>

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.080
Major?

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.870
Shit. Saito!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.810
Don't kill him!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.030
It's over, buddy!

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:26.040
Damn, it feels gross having someone infiltrate my Ghost. Even the Major.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.370
Quoted for truth...

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.210
Your fault for aiming for the head.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.570
Don't hand them over yet.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.780
We'll take them to a lockup with cyber facilities.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.760
You telling me to play interrogation partner?

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.930
I'm not interested in fake memories.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.930
Memories?

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:44.150
I'm interested in their contaminated Ghosts.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.950
Sorry I had to call you down here.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:59.170
It's my civic duty.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:01.410
I understand you're in charge of the dam.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:02.900
Let's see...

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.120
Dr. Zhinzhee Bekka Arr Thied.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.910
Please, call me Thied.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.910
You've got quite the tough-looking secretary.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.340
He's very reliable.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:19.340
The conflicts continue in the Republic of Kuzan, where you're from.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:25.060
I hear the Qhardi ethnic minority in particular is still waging a war of independence.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.020
It's a heartbreaking war.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.480
You're Qhardi, correct?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:36.080
Yes. Like the majority of my comrades, I wish for a peaceful solution.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.920
So, the explosion at the dam...

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.410
I'm told it was a valve malfunction.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:45.880
Your company sells water, right?

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.580
For what type of use?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.750
It's for precision machinery businesses.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:53.620
That industry relies on 100% pure water.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.380
Precision machinery...

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.530
Prosthetic manufacturing, for example?

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:58.270
Yes.

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:01.790
Chief.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:04.760
You idiot!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.560
The Trade Ministry got them invited to set up a plant here!

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.190
You want to make an enemy of the local precinct too?

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.470
But...

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:19.310
Stop, that's evidence!

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:25.830
I'm very grateful to you for finding
 the goods stolen from our warehouse.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:27.760
Please, take them with you.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.770
Chief!

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:30.730
Back off!

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.180
A detective died, sir.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:35.790
You think I don't know that?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:38.760
You go to Nishinouchi and get me information.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.250
Nishinouchi? What's there?

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:45.280
A bombing, apparently by Qhardi terrorists.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.360
Now listen. You consult your superiors before any moves on this case.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.090
Terrorism?

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:54.730
If the explosion was intentional, and he wasn't a victim...

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:56.880
What?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.100
Yes, sir! I'm on it!

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.110
Don't make any trouble!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.580
They're a Qhardi weapons smuggling gang.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.790
I met them on an undercover op.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:16.660
Their goal is to send weapons to their comrades back home.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:18.950
They've got no reason to attack this country.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.020
Their statements were crystal clear.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:24.800
They're against the pricing agreement, so they bombed the meeting site.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.880
Are you telling me those are planted memories?

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.270
I'm betting they're all infected,

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.270
and that the virus interfered with my ghost lock.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.280
Well done. You subdued them brilliantly.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:47.240
We could do it even more easily if you 
adjusted your comm standards to ours.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.410
I read your report.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:54.750
A false memory virus that can infiltrate, hack, and brainwash simultaneously?

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.710
It's a self-destructing Stuxnet-type.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.710
Other than the symptoms at its onset, it leaves no trace.

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:04.920
Electronic manipulation of memory is incredibly difficult.

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.280
No one in the world has been confirmed successful.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:11.600
And yet past incidents tell us a 
maker and a broker clearly exist.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:16.730
Yes. Somewhere out there is the super-wizard-class programmer

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:19.520
known as "Fire-Starter" who 
created this high-level cyber-virus.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:23.440
Until now, no organization in the world had uncovered his identity.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:24.490
But you did?

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.450
A clue, anyway.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:33.370
What's this?

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.660
All the terrorists had the same tattoo.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:42.050
It's a symbol used by Scylla, the hero who once led the Qhardi Separatist Army.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.750
I've heard of him.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.170
Word is he's a master of cyber warfare.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.970
Is he Fire-Starter?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.550
No way. He died during the war.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.110
You're going to find out whether that's true.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:56.350
I'll authorize limited access to Section 9's database.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.070
Read the details there.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.020
That's all?

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.580
You're complaining?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.490
I gave you all the Logicomas I have, plus 
our weapons and permission to use them.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:09.950
Any lists I make are meaningless if the organization can't act.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.640
And?

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.900
I want special authority and an approved budget.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:19.220
And make your flimsy comm lines backward compatible with ours while you're at it.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:21.380
Enough!

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:25.010
Your team isn't regulation size,
 and I'm graciously turning a blind eye!

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.200
This unit is standardized to the perfect specs.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.000
We don't need more people.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.930
Then the whole unit will go down the second you get hacked.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.800
Just like those terrorists did.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.690
Your "perfect specs" don't merit my trust.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:41.060
If you want authority and a budget,

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:45.540
get at least one more member and accept 
cooperation from someone with different specs.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:52.410
If they won't give us money, we're 
stuck in this garbage dump for a while.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.450
I'm just glad we've got a lab to use.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:02.630
Yeah, high prosthetic performance takes superior maintenance...

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.490
We'll have to pay for upgrades out of pocket.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.800
Costs a lot, though.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.470
Training ground instructors make pretty good money.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.510
Top-quality maintenance facilities, authority—we'll get it all.

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.480
Stop wasting time bitching and solve our case!

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.940
His nationality's unknown.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.920
He uses multiple bodies to conceal
 his identity, earning the name Skulla,

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.830
aka Scylla.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.410
That's the name of a monster from Greek mythology.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.800
A pro at warfare who led a separatist army, and whiz hacker...

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.460
Huh, his specialty is tunnel ops.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.620
"Tunnel ops"?

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:47.090
That's when you bomb someplace's lifelines and then infiltrate them electronically during their restoration.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:51.660
Ultimately you wage a destructive 
cyber-attack from inside their defenses.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:56.220
The forces who tried to prevent 
independence took a major hit instead.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:02.560
But Kuzan joined forces with advanced nations to 
manipulate the Qhardis in order to contain its neighbors.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:07.190
It was a throwaway war of independence, and this country was especially involved.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:12.360
No one recognized the Qhardis' independence after the war, and the guerrillas were disbanded and slaughtered.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:18.680
But their dead leader was actually alive, and he developed a special virus ahead of all the world's research institutions,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:22.350
then changed his name to Fire-Starter and began his revenge...

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.500
I follow the logic, but is it really possible?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:29.080
In a conflict zone, you can do all the human experimentation you want.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:30.770
It's no wonder, really.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:32.970
Scylla is dead.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.300
A successor of his, then?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:38.990
Either way, the broker isn't peddling it without knowing what it does.

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:44.690
So he wanted to use those guerrillas to repeat his old tunnel operation here?

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.470
It bothers me that no one was carrying a detonator.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.750
Borma, check out the crime scene.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:52.680
Roger.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:57.160
Paz, you and Saito pay the gang a visit. I want to know who trained them.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.330
Batou and Ishikawa, you look into the possibility of a tunnel op.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.830
Do you plan to dive into the guerrillas' cyberbrains looking for the virus?

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:09.560
I'll get a tune-up on my body first.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.720
A tune-up?

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:18.260
It's her boyfriend. He's an ex-military prosthetics tech.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.000
Isn't he a Navy sailor?

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.560
That was the last one.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:25.270
They fought on a date, and she kicked his
 ass hard enough to put him in the hospital.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:28.680
What about that rich one from the Cyberbrain Bureau?

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.860
He didn't last two weeks.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.820
So this is the sixth in six months? She's got a sickness.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:37.360
No, it's instinct. I never sleep with the same woman twice either.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:40.280
Because you always end up a hostage or a target for revenge?

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.910
No, because it's my policy.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:46.020
At least do a quick background check! What if one of them's a trap?

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.590
It's better than hearing, "I want a family".

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.930
Yeah, after all, you could die at any time.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:53.590
This is no job for a family man.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.960
So the late detective's gun wasn't found?

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:05.530
If Detective Mizuki had fired his weapon,

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:08.310
it would prove this was a crime, and not an accident.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.020
You think someone wanted it to look like an accident?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.280
The cause of death was drowning, 
but he lost a lot of blood antemortem,

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.990
and some of his bones are missing.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:24.200
So the body's too damaged to tell, but he may have been shot.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.600
Detective Mizuki was investigating weapons smuggling.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.570
His most recent meeting was with a Qhardi organization.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.960
I suspect he was killed because he found proof.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:39.930
You feel the dam explosion was intentional, set up to bury evidence?

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.810
You've got a very active imagination.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.110
You're turning me down, sir?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:47.770
No, I like it. I'll allow you to investigate.

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:50.480
Try to find a connection between the incidents.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.470
All alone?

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.230
You're complaining?

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:56.200
I appreciate it, sir!

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.920
Humans can never perfectly reproduce movements.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:09.050
A slight slope, our distance from our target, a few milligrams' weight difference...

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:13.690
The brain calculates all these things to create yet-unknown movements.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:18.520
You have the most original brain I know of, and
 you understand the beauty of uniform standards.

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:22.140
You're exaggerating.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.790
There's nothing wrong with you.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.100
It still hurts?

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.100
Try moving your right leg.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:34.670
Lovely.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.080
What's "lovely"?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.180
Your leg.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.450
The pain is gone now.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:47.130
Send me a bill.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:50.490
I'll give you a discount. In return, don't forget our promise.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:52.280
You're a strange man.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.630
Not as strange as you.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.690
Hey, you. You're blocking my scan.

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:12.270
Oh, sorry.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:16.100
What good are your natural eyes in the cyber age?

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:19.140
It's not normally this hard to find the epicenter.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:22.040
You know a lot about the combustion process?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.640
I learned the basics overseas during the war.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:25.990
I see.

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.490
Are you a full cyborg?

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.140
Yeah, pretty close.

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:37.300
I'm no expert, but unless you get a specialized skeleton, aren't the basics the same as a human body's?

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:40.200
But his hands stayed open after he burned...

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:40.960
What?

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:47.220
When a natural human burns to death, his muscles contract, so he forms fists and he bends forward.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.080
The fetal position, or, you know, the boxer's pose.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:51.870
Heat rigor?

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:52.930
Well, what about it?

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.410
This guard's corpse

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:59.360
is standing up straight, hands open.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.870
Must be some property of his prosthetics, or of the bomb.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:03.720
Prosthetics?

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.410
Hello?

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.750
Oh, a checkup?

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:16.720
Two weeks?

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:18.480
Got it.

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:21.340
No, I'm working right now, sorry.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:22.760
"Checkup"?

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.510
Sorry to bother you.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.900
C-4 and dynamite, glycerin, and chemical fertilizer...

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:41.160
It's a hideout straight out of a book.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.710
Definitely a bomb maniac vibe.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.820
But I've got no clue what they actually used.

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.780
Orders coming down their line!

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:54.500
Someone calling himself Scylla just ordered some "Second Army" into action.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.710
Damn bastards! Public Security's moves are being leaked!

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:06.870
The Waterworks Bureau's server blew, and took out the whole floor.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.240
What did they use?

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:13.280
The accelerant at the Nishinouchi crime scene is spread all the way to the ceiling, even the ducts.

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:17.790
We're talking omnidirectional blast. The air itself blew up.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:18.980
A fuel-air explosive?

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.840
Then this is a dummy hideout.

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:23.940
They've got a more advanced bomb lab somewhere.

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:31.870
Damn guerrilla hero is issuing a challenge.

00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:40.790
The Waterworks Bureau is starting repairs.

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:43.800
Odds are the hacker's already in!

00:22:43.800 --> 00:22:45.620
Figure out their next target.

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:47.520
Don't let them dig any more tunnels.

00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:09.320
I appreciate your cooperation.

00:23:10.060 --> 00:23:12.320
I'm used to police questioning.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.780
There've been a lot of prosthetics thefts recently.

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:18.290
"Mermaid's Legs", eh?

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:21.500
Not a very artistic name, but it's easy to understand.

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:24.020
My female customers quite like it.

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.210
Do you recognize these legs?

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:30.380
They appear to be the mass-production model.

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:32.250
Look at the tag.

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:35.310
"Ariel".

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:39.600
I've asked around, and there's no such model on the market.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:41.220
I don't carry it, either.

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:43.270
It must be a licensed designer's brand name.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:48.430
Designers use the mass-production model as a base and then innovate to meet customer demands.

00:23:48.430 --> 00:23:49.610
Any ideas?

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.320
I'll give you my list.

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:54.150
One moment, please.

00:23:55.180 --> 00:23:56.240
Thank you.

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:06.960
Cops love lists.

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:09.280
He'll be conveniently absorbed in it for a while.

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:11.840
Public Security took our dummy safe house.

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:15.140
Are the comm lines here safe, Colonel Hozumi?

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:18.640
Don't worry. It's one of Intelligence's independent lines.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:21.100
Why haven't you killed that detective?

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:24.060
He's an odd duck, but he doesn't have any powerful backers.

00:24:24.620 --> 00:24:26.790
The real issue is that Ariel's been leaked.

00:24:26.790 --> 00:24:30.960
We retrieved the sample before it was analyzed, and the factory is taken care of.

00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:33.310
I didn't expect you to panic and blow it up.

00:24:33.310 --> 00:24:36.370
We're lucky Ariel was mounted in time.

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:39.290
You almost seriously hindered our plan.

00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:43.250
Ariel is a way to smuggle explosives to the Qhardis!

00:24:43.700 --> 00:24:44.830
It's not for suicide bombers!

00:24:45.650 --> 00:24:47.450
Circumstances have changed.

00:24:47.450 --> 00:24:53.050
If previous overseas weapons development becomes domestic, distribution channels will vanish.

00:24:53.550 --> 00:24:55.510
The Qhardi soldiers are just sacrificial pawns?

00:24:55.850 --> 00:24:57.320
We're upgrading.

00:24:57.320 --> 00:25:00.880
Fire-Starter can create all the soldiers we want.

00:25:00.880 --> 00:25:03.230
Get the unit that was arrested released.

00:25:03.850 --> 00:25:05.760
I won't give you the data until then.

00:25:06.750 --> 00:25:08.690
They aren't even your compatriots.

00:25:09.340 --> 00:25:11.860
Scylla would never abandon them.

00:25:13.720 --> 00:25:17.620
Very well. There are three more usable Ariels.

00:25:17.970 --> 00:25:20.580
One of them is in your court.

00:25:21.490 --> 00:25:23.040
It really has to be her?

00:25:23.530 --> 00:25:25.240
Developed feelings for her, have we?

00:25:25.240 --> 00:25:27.250
Activate the woman's Ariel.

00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:30.500
Release our allies first. Understand?

00:25:56.130 --> 00:25:57.030
Ride with me.

00:26:03.510 --> 00:26:07.470
You haven't told anyone that you and I killed Scylla, I trust?

00:26:07.470 --> 00:26:08.490
No.

00:26:08.490 --> 00:26:11.240
That op is a stain on both our records.

00:26:11.240 --> 00:26:13.890
It would be highly inconvenient for it to come up again now.

00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:17.930
I see you dived happily into the power games as soon as you made LTC.

00:26:18.530 --> 00:26:22.580
They used the military-industrial complex to profit from death.

00:26:22.580 --> 00:26:28.780
I'll wipe them out, make domestic weapons engineering big, and shut down their trade routes to foreign cartels.

00:26:28.780 --> 00:26:31.150
Lt. Col. Mamuro wanted that.

00:26:31.590 --> 00:26:33.820
I won't play your game.

00:26:34.220 --> 00:26:36.890
Scylla is a game you can't quit.

00:26:36.890 --> 00:26:38.990
She has to stay dead.

00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:41.530
You used this before.

00:26:42.740 --> 00:26:46.190
Bury it and whoever's using Scylla's name—permanently this time.

00:26:46.190 --> 00:26:49.720
Or else the brass will bury <i>you</i>, along with that op.

00:26:58.200 --> 00:27:01.640
Becoming independent of the system doesn't make you free.

00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:06.060
You're like last century's programmers, who 
expected too much from the birth of the Net.

00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:10.440
Even Section 9 is only letting you have your own way to test you.

00:27:10.440 --> 00:27:14.620
When they need to, they'll restrain you with a Ghost infiltration key and dispose of you.

00:27:14.620 --> 00:27:17.930
I have no intention of letting
 anyone infiltrate my Ghost again.

00:27:17.930 --> 00:27:19.780
No matter who they are.

00:27:26.470 --> 00:27:28.560
That woman is Kusanagi Motoko?

00:27:29.260 --> 00:27:31.180
Yes, your senior.

00:27:31.180 --> 00:27:32.210
Can you win?

00:27:35.780 --> 00:27:37.530
If you wish.

00:28:03.860 --> 00:28:05.620
You really came?

00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:07.700
I did promise.

00:28:08.630 --> 00:28:10.470
I haven't prepared anything.

00:28:10.470 --> 00:28:11.660
I figured.

00:28:18.300 --> 00:28:20.550
But first, we'll take care of this.

00:28:32.340 --> 00:28:37.240
I checked out the Qhardi gang, but there's no trace of their tactical commander.

00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:40.570
Ah, but I've got the rental server they used.

00:28:41.230 --> 00:28:43.410
Multiple invaders into a public facility...

00:28:43.410 --> 00:28:45.600
Bastards have made good progress on their tunnels.

00:28:45.600 --> 00:28:47.530
Do you know where they're going yet?

00:28:47.840 --> 00:28:50.430
It's someplace to do with water and precision machinery.

00:28:50.430 --> 00:28:53.400
78 places in the city fit that description.

00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:55.040
Check them all.

00:28:55.780 --> 00:29:00.000
Damn... I'd make easier money being an Intelligence subcontractor.

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:03.090
So, still in your "tune-up"?

00:29:03.090 --> 00:29:05.470
Yes. I'm dropping this connection for a while.

00:29:06.490 --> 00:29:08.360
I can hear noise.

00:29:08.360 --> 00:29:11.800
Your coworkers are in and out of your lobby nonstop, huh?

00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:13.310
I ran them all off.

00:29:13.730 --> 00:29:16.270
You think I'll ever get to be in your lobby?

00:29:17.490 --> 00:29:19.970
If you work with me.

00:29:19.970 --> 00:29:22.940
If I said I needed one more person, would you come?

00:29:25.110 --> 00:29:27.700
Tuning you up whenever I want is an attractive proposition,

00:29:28.610 --> 00:29:31.030
but I don't get involved with the military or the police.

00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:32.910
Oh.

00:29:36.260 --> 00:29:38.360
I did some first aid on your sensory components.

00:29:38.360 --> 00:29:40.000
Let's do the detail work in the lab.

00:29:41.020 --> 00:29:42.800
The pain is gone.

00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:44.380
I'll do the rest myself.

00:29:48.890 --> 00:29:50.220
Then let's get started.

00:29:57.240 --> 00:29:59.560
I remember when I first met you, you know.

00:30:00.620 --> 00:30:05.280
All the other engineers said you were the queen of customer complaints.

00:30:05.550 --> 00:30:07.990
Is that why they handed me off to a freelancer like you?

00:30:08.680 --> 00:30:10.950
Nope. The truth is, I asked them to.

00:30:11.780 --> 00:30:12.460
What?

00:30:13.820 --> 00:30:19.880
You couldn't decide whether you should treat your body as a thing or a person.

00:30:21.220 --> 00:30:23.070
That made me interested in you.

00:30:29.520 --> 00:30:34.720
At the facility I was in before, they thought I was an
 oddball for wanting to sleep in a bed and take showers.

00:30:35.270 --> 00:30:38.210
When I was prosthetized on the battlefield, they told me,

00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:41.730
"A cyborg doesn't need everyday life; he needs equipment."

00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:44.900
That's why I switched to prosthetics engineering.

00:30:46.170 --> 00:30:49.360
I wanted to be a tech who'd treat cyborgs like humans.

00:30:51.110 --> 00:30:55.870
As a kid, they gave me everyday-living training outside the facility.

00:30:55.870 --> 00:30:58.330
So I'd learn how to be more human.

00:30:59.260 --> 00:31:00.830
I don't really remember it.

00:31:01.710 --> 00:31:03.580
Everything was so bright...

00:31:04.460 --> 00:31:07.160
I remember I came back ahead of schedule.

00:31:09.150 --> 00:31:13.390
But... that day I decided to make my body orthodox.

00:31:13.820 --> 00:31:15.920
I wanted to look human.

00:31:15.920 --> 00:31:18.130
Your prosthetic body isn't a thing.

00:31:18.130 --> 00:31:19.910
It's your real body.

00:31:19.910 --> 00:31:23.150
It mustn't be treated as a thing... Not by anyone.

00:31:24.900 --> 00:31:26.100
Not by me.

00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:29.980
I do wish that were true.

00:31:29.980 --> 00:31:31.680
I'll show you proof.

00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:32.780
Proof?

00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:37.370
It's a surprise.

00:31:40.930 --> 00:31:42.830
We're missing the key piece: the bomb.

00:31:43.130 --> 00:31:47.040
How did they get it into a heavily guarded meeting place?

00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:48.050
What about the perps?

00:31:48.050 --> 00:31:50.510
They say they're the ones who blew it up.

00:31:51.020 --> 00:31:53.970
Despite the fact that they have no memory of the bomb.

00:31:53.970 --> 00:31:57.710
They're fall guys. They probably 
have nothing to do with the bomb.

00:31:57.710 --> 00:32:01.840
We'll monitor all 78 locations until we can narrow down their target.

00:32:01.840 --> 00:32:03.580
Are you serious?!

00:32:03.580 --> 00:32:05.330
Contact me if something happens.

00:32:09.070 --> 00:32:10.640
You're wearing heels.

00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:14.260
Should we assume the ex-military 
prosthetics tech is joining the team?

00:32:18.140 --> 00:32:19.880
Maybe that's actually for real.

00:32:31.550 --> 00:32:33.470
This is what you wanted to show me?

00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:35.890
They're regular customers of mine.

00:32:36.260 --> 00:32:38.350
Their average age is 70.

00:32:39.550 --> 00:32:41.310
They're all full-body cyborgs...

00:32:41.660 --> 00:32:45.240
The affluent elderly are at the core of cyborg development these days.

00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:46.520
Not soldiers.

00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:51.240
They want prosthetic bodies to give them second lives, and fulfilling lifestyles.

00:32:52.220 --> 00:32:56.120
More and more foods for cyborgs are being developed to meet their needs, too.

00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:04.950
Try it.

00:33:17.820 --> 00:33:18.850
It's good.

00:33:19.560 --> 00:33:21.950
Is it your first time allocating memory to your sense of taste?

00:33:23.910 --> 00:33:26.270
The new bride is pregnant, by the way.

00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:29.560
Exciting, isn't it?

00:33:29.560 --> 00:33:33.280
A new world of humans that don't
 distinguish between prosthetic and flesh.

00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:37.100
You really are strange.

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:47.860
Some people reject the future.

00:33:47.860 --> 00:33:51.460
And some are left behind by it too.

00:33:55.420 --> 00:33:58.630
I want to bring the cyborg future to the third world.

00:34:00.890 --> 00:34:02.290
Will you come with me?

00:34:04.140 --> 00:34:06.900
You should use your power freely,

00:34:07.740 --> 00:34:10.690
not work under a bunch of puppet masters.

00:34:13.190 --> 00:34:15.330
The war is over, you know.

00:34:15.330 --> 00:34:17.010
No, it's still going.

00:34:17.010 --> 00:34:20.440
The nations it grew inconvenient for pulled out, that's all.

00:34:23.620 --> 00:34:26.590
I have things to do in this country.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:28.950
I see.

00:34:29.820 --> 00:34:31.420
Do you have free time later?

00:34:31.420 --> 00:34:35.260
If we share a lobby, we can meet whenever we want.

00:34:35.260 --> 00:34:37.380
I might touch your Ghost.

00:34:37.380 --> 00:34:39.410
I'll let down my barrier.

00:34:39.410 --> 00:34:40.360
Are you sure?

00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:43.000
If you infiltrate me, I may fry your brain.

00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:44.690
It might be worth it.

00:35:07.920 --> 00:35:09.500
This is your body.

00:35:11.710 --> 00:35:13.540
These are your hands.

00:35:39.360 --> 00:35:40.870
Motoko, run!

00:36:16.160 --> 00:36:16.860
Akira!

00:36:19.030 --> 00:36:19.840
Are you all right?

00:36:21.110 --> 00:36:22.450
Yeah...

00:36:30.790 --> 00:36:32.040
I'm sorry.

00:36:32.040 --> 00:36:33.370
This is my fault.

00:37:12.320 --> 00:37:13.620
Sorry to hear what happened.

00:37:14.910 --> 00:37:16.830
Paz is with Section 9 inspecting the scene.

00:37:17.540 --> 00:37:20.050
Your attacker was a pro, even if he did mess up.

00:37:20.580 --> 00:37:22.770
It's unclear whether this was tied to the bombing,

00:37:22.770 --> 00:37:25.600
but we'd normally give you police protection at this point.

00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:26.850
I don't need it.

00:37:26.850 --> 00:37:28.000
How is he?

00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.480
We'll send him home as soon as we're done questioning him.

00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:32.520
I'll assign someone to him, so don't worry.

00:37:32.520 --> 00:37:33.770
I see.

00:37:33.770 --> 00:37:37.100
The military authorities won't give me any information on Scylla.

00:37:37.100 --> 00:37:38.890
What's your connection to him?

00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:43.490
Call me whenever you need help.

00:37:47.350 --> 00:37:49.400
Scylla's revenge, eh?

00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:51.450
Good thing your boyfriend's a civilian.

00:37:51.790 --> 00:37:53.630
We don't have to suspect a leak.

00:37:55.820 --> 00:37:56.790
They got us.

00:37:57.420 --> 00:38:00.800
Number three: a materials control center on the coast.

00:38:01.260 --> 00:38:05.490
I picked up a go order in Scylla's name 30 seconds before the explosion.

00:38:05.490 --> 00:38:07.050
Then the whole line disappeared.

00:38:07.050 --> 00:38:09.130
Is there even any point in surveillance?

00:38:09.130 --> 00:38:13.020
Find a weapons engineer on their 
customer list who's connected to this.

00:38:13.020 --> 00:38:14.390
Weapons engineer?

00:38:14.390 --> 00:38:16.520
Get info from the first victims, too. Hurry up.

00:38:17.020 --> 00:38:19.490
Find something. The virus, the bombs, the tactical commander,

00:38:19.490 --> 00:38:23.690
where the messages from "Scylla" come from—I don't care what.

00:38:24.290 --> 00:38:29.410
How about you finally tell us why you're so sure Scylla's dead?

00:38:30.180 --> 00:38:30.830
Excuse me.

00:38:32.880 --> 00:38:34.000
You!

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:36.990
I was told I could find Major Kusanagi here.

00:38:36.990 --> 00:38:37.840
What is it?

00:38:44.290 --> 00:38:45.710
State your business.

00:38:45.710 --> 00:38:49.060
The list I got from him was a fake.

00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:54.680
And a detective working a weapons trafficking 
case was killed right after getting info from him.

00:38:55.070 --> 00:39:01.150
Techs get blamed for prosthetics-related incidents all the time.

00:39:02.030 --> 00:39:05.020
And the manager of the dam that exploded the other day...

00:39:06.510 --> 00:39:08.470
Hose outfitted her bodyguard, too.

00:39:08.470 --> 00:39:09.860
So what?!

00:39:10.740 --> 00:39:13.830
How did you feel, watching your 
lover get attacked in front of you?

00:39:15.690 --> 00:39:19.400
You're angry at the perp, and you feel guilty.

00:39:19.400 --> 00:39:21.790
You think it was your fault he got attacked.

00:39:25.110 --> 00:39:27.080
He was the same way.

00:39:27.080 --> 00:39:28.800
Anger and guilt.

00:39:29.370 --> 00:39:31.430
He's hiding something.

00:39:31.430 --> 00:39:35.760
The dam, the dead detective, 
the prosthetics, and even you, Major...

00:39:36.490 --> 00:39:38.590
Everything links back to Hose Akira.

00:39:42.460 --> 00:39:45.000
You're just a cheap detective 
snooping around with flesh eyes!

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:46.610
Never show your face here again!

00:39:51.010 --> 00:39:53.070
Ouch...

00:40:14.580 --> 00:40:16.260
You're a fool, Colonel!

00:40:18.650 --> 00:40:20.090
An attack barrier!

00:40:20.090 --> 00:40:21.230
Keep calm.

00:40:21.860 --> 00:40:26.990
If the domestic faction takes away your arms industry rights, you'll be killed by the cartels.

00:40:26.990 --> 00:40:30.390
Yet you're in a rush to kill me off and steal my data?

00:40:30.390 --> 00:40:34.200
So, you act like a heavyweight, but you couldn't get my people released?

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:36.370
Where is the data?

00:40:36.790 --> 00:40:38.470
Our deal is over.

00:40:38.470 --> 00:40:44.480
I'm thankful for the info on her and for
 Scylla's revival, but I'm leaving this country.

00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:45.960
You do the same.

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:47.670
No need.

00:40:53.590 --> 00:40:57.600
We've successfully packaged the virus with cyberbrains.

00:40:59.970 --> 00:41:03.440
We'll use your cyberbrain for the final upgrade.

00:41:03.740 --> 00:41:05.900
Become Scylla, just like you wanted to.

00:41:15.070 --> 00:41:18.590
"His hands stayed open after he burned", eh?

00:41:39.660 --> 00:41:41.110
It's just like the call said.

00:41:41.110 --> 00:41:44.180
Two Public Security officers killed, 
and Hose Akira's whereabouts unknown.

00:41:44.480 --> 00:41:46.280
The Major wasn't the target?

00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:48.270
Hey, look at this list.

00:41:48.270 --> 00:41:53.880
It's only a guess, but I think the FAEs 
were the prosthetic limbs themselves.

00:41:53.880 --> 00:41:57.300
There was another full-cyborg 
guard in that part of the building.

00:41:57.300 --> 00:42:00.240
The limbs' admin records have the same signature on them...

00:42:03.590 --> 00:42:05.080
What are you doing?

00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:09.420
Who is this man?!

00:42:14.210 --> 00:42:17.040
My attack barrier expands every second.

00:42:17.040 --> 00:42:18.800
If you don't want your brain fried, tell me!

00:42:18.800 --> 00:42:20.550
He'll die!

00:42:21.180 --> 00:42:23.560
He gave us power...

00:42:23.560 --> 00:42:25.560
He's Scylla reborn!

00:42:26.020 --> 00:42:28.000
It was like magic.

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:31.890
A battle-learning program left to us by the dead Scylla...

00:42:31.890 --> 00:42:35.560
He gave it to my cyberbrain, along with the virus.

00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:39.910
I'd never been trained, but now I can fight even your people!

00:42:39.910 --> 00:42:41.370
Give me a name.

00:42:41.980 --> 00:42:43.630
Hose Akira!

00:42:43.630 --> 00:42:45.830
He's Japanese, like you!

00:42:54.290 --> 00:42:55.420
Hose escaped.

00:42:56.020 --> 00:42:57.050
Any idea where?

00:42:57.050 --> 00:42:58.590
Why ask me?

00:42:58.590 --> 00:43:01.350
What are your eyes looking at right now?

00:43:03.270 --> 00:43:05.310
Zhinzhee Bekka Arr Thied.

00:43:06.110 --> 00:43:12.230
She's boss of a Kuzan water company, 
and most likely the weapons ring's sponsor.

00:43:12.230 --> 00:43:14.480
So this is the tunnel exit!

00:43:15.110 --> 00:43:18.150
A domestic weapons company. Harimadara Heavy Industries!

00:43:18.940 --> 00:43:22.370
The execs are touring Factory One with the Senior Vice-Minister of Defense!

00:43:22.910 --> 00:43:26.040
Recommend a barrier, and give the data to Section 9.

00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:28.290
Paz, Borma, Saito, get over there.

00:43:31.090 --> 00:43:34.160
Call the bomb squad and a prosthetics tech.

00:43:34.160 --> 00:43:36.760
A destructive cyber-attack is more than likely.

00:43:41.340 --> 00:43:43.900
What's the meaning of this, Chief Aramaki?

00:43:43.900 --> 00:43:45.310
Evacuate immediately.

00:43:45.820 --> 00:43:48.270
You and this facility are targets.

00:43:48.860 --> 00:43:50.730
Wh-What's going on?!

00:43:54.510 --> 00:43:56.190
It's a bomb! Run!

00:44:02.200 --> 00:44:03.190
Damn.

00:44:03.190 --> 00:44:04.210
Shit!

00:44:04.210 --> 00:44:05.200
Paz, Borma!

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:06.660
This way!

00:44:09.550 --> 00:44:11.330
Help me! Help me!

00:44:20.190 --> 00:44:22.710
Crap, the fire's closing up my throat.

00:44:22.710 --> 00:44:25.180
Mine too. That was close.

00:44:26.060 --> 00:44:27.830
Vice-Minister, are you all right?

00:44:27.830 --> 00:44:29.460
I'm fine.

00:44:35.410 --> 00:44:36.180
Logicoma.

00:44:36.820 --> 00:44:37.570
Yes, sir!

00:44:40.140 --> 00:44:42.030
That's one of our products!

00:44:45.450 --> 00:44:46.530
Away from the windows!

00:44:51.780 --> 00:44:54.040
That's all the info on Colonel Hozumi.

00:44:54.040 --> 00:44:55.480
That's fine.

00:44:55.480 --> 00:44:58.750
We get a card, and you get a grace period.

00:44:59.140 --> 00:45:02.470
Please tell me what she has to do with Scylla!

00:45:02.880 --> 00:45:04.500
Find out from her.

00:45:04.500 --> 00:45:09.810
Your contaminated brain is intriguing, but I'm 
cutting our connection before the infection spreads.

00:45:15.060 --> 00:45:16.150
Goodbye.

00:45:26.060 --> 00:45:27.620
Contaminated, eh?

00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:31.120
I'm being bankrupted by a special tax on foreign companies?!

00:45:31.740 --> 00:45:34.150
How can this be allowed?!

00:45:34.150 --> 00:45:36.830
It's the kind of thing the domestic faction would do.

00:45:37.930 --> 00:45:39.040
What do you plan to do?

00:45:39.980 --> 00:45:41.450
Kill the colonel?

00:45:42.010 --> 00:45:45.030
She's all washed up. And so are you and l.

00:45:52.460 --> 00:45:54.350
Escape, and obey the domestic faction.

00:45:55.190 --> 00:45:59.060
Your company will be crushed under the pretext of this nation's taxes.

00:45:59.650 --> 00:46:01.600
You'll be killed by the cartels if you don't do something.

00:46:04.750 --> 00:46:06.440
You okay, Major?

00:46:06.440 --> 00:46:07.770
No problems.

00:46:07.770 --> 00:46:10.740
You go with that detective and subdue the guards.

00:46:11.680 --> 00:46:14.960
I'll take care of Scylla.

00:46:20.300 --> 00:46:22.420
Jeez, so stubborn. That's a scary lady.

00:46:28.160 --> 00:46:28.800
What?

00:46:29.520 --> 00:46:31.180
A Mateba, in this day and age?

00:46:31.180 --> 00:46:32.510
What's wrong with that?!

00:46:32.510 --> 00:46:34.370
I trust this gun more than any other.

00:46:45.250 --> 00:46:46.320
Blood traces.

00:46:46.770 --> 00:46:48.240
Someone was shot.

00:46:54.630 --> 00:46:55.500
A bullet...

00:47:14.290 --> 00:47:17.210
Ariel. So these are the prosthetic bombs.

00:47:35.950 --> 00:47:37.910
That wasn't you just now.

00:47:37.910 --> 00:47:40.500
Who the hell infiltrated my vision?!

00:47:40.840 --> 00:47:41.630
Don't move!

00:47:44.460 --> 00:47:49.930
In that quagmire of a war, Scylla was 
the only soldier I could empathize with.

00:47:50.430 --> 00:47:53.640
I've always wanted to ask you why he was killed.

00:47:55.310 --> 00:47:57.680
You didn't kill Scylla.

00:47:57.680 --> 00:47:59.100
I finally realized that.

00:48:01.840 --> 00:48:02.950
Go home.

00:48:02.950 --> 00:48:05.480
Or your Ariel will activate.

00:48:06.750 --> 00:48:08.110
Even I can't stop it.

00:48:33.840 --> 00:48:34.920
What's going on here?

00:48:34.920 --> 00:48:39.120
That bastard infiltrated my vision exactly the way you do!

00:48:39.120 --> 00:48:40.480
Answer me, Major!

00:48:58.660 --> 00:49:00.440
What's taking the Army so long?!

00:49:00.440 --> 00:49:02.120
We'll all die like this!

00:49:02.450 --> 00:49:04.240
It's been seized.

00:49:04.240 --> 00:49:07.380
It won't stop until we shut down whatever it's packaged with.

00:49:07.380 --> 00:49:09.120
Transplanted memories.

00:49:09.120 --> 00:49:09.960
What?

00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:13.180
The packaged cyberbrains are the virus' hosts.

00:49:13.820 --> 00:49:17.680
They converted the tactical program I set loose in Qhardistan to memory.

00:49:18.110 --> 00:49:19.600
My copy.

00:49:24.020 --> 00:49:25.810
What the hell are you saying?!

00:49:34.240 --> 00:49:35.100
<i>Motoko.</i>

00:50:03.520 --> 00:50:07.310
I came after you, but in the end, you captured me.

00:50:09.210 --> 00:50:11.880
It was my cyberbrain that was packaged.

00:50:11.880 --> 00:50:14.960
If you pull the trigger, you and your comrades will be saved.

00:50:18.890 --> 00:50:21.070
What you fell in love with was this world.

00:50:25.340 --> 00:50:28.540
Just keep on going, until the day you're betrayed.

00:50:33.260 --> 00:50:34.230
Scylla...

00:50:35.660 --> 00:50:37.130
I'm glad I met you.

00:51:05.440 --> 00:51:06.280
What?

00:51:07.100 --> 00:51:08.490
It stopped...

00:51:17.910 --> 00:51:19.300
It's ironic.

00:51:19.300 --> 00:51:21.610
They manage to survive a world war,

00:51:21.610 --> 00:51:26.080
then get stuck in an endless one, and finally end their own lives.

00:51:26.080 --> 00:51:28.610
Apparently there's no other way they can stop.

00:51:29.420 --> 00:51:31.270
Weren't you the same?

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:35.250
Scylla was you.

00:51:35.250 --> 00:51:38.750
You helped the separatist army, then faked your death.

00:51:38.750 --> 00:51:41.740
Later, the guerrillas you led were all killed.

00:51:42.560 --> 00:51:44.810
I can see why you wouldn't want to remember that op.

00:51:46.590 --> 00:51:49.770
Since then, I've stopped switching bodies so often.

00:51:50.680 --> 00:51:52.710
It gives me an identity crisis.

00:51:53.140 --> 00:51:55.670
I lose track of who I am,

00:51:55.670 --> 00:51:59.650
and then I want someone to tell me I'm not a robot.

00:52:03.100 --> 00:52:06.680
Is that why you insist on making original tweaks to your mass-production bases?

00:52:07.450 --> 00:52:11.100
It's amazing you even managed to control so many bodies in such a short time.

00:52:11.520 --> 00:52:12.950
I'm going to sleep a little.

00:52:12.950 --> 00:52:14.110
You can go.

00:52:14.650 --> 00:52:16.570
Call it cyborg solidarity.

00:52:16.570 --> 00:52:19.610
I'll keep watch and make sure they 
don't fit you with any sketchy parts.

00:52:20.300 --> 00:52:22.540
All right, suit yourself.

00:52:23.940 --> 00:52:26.030
You could at least say "thanks"!

00:52:29.810 --> 00:52:33.170
The bullet at the scene was fired from the lieutenant's gun.

00:52:33.820 --> 00:52:36.680
I also found Mizuki's weapon at the lieutenant's home.

00:52:36.680 --> 00:52:39.130
There was a huge deposit into his account, too.

00:52:43.160 --> 00:52:44.050
Good work.

00:52:44.540 --> 00:52:45.630
You can go.

00:52:57.660 --> 00:53:00.240
Arresting a fellow cop will make you some enemies.

00:53:03.180 --> 00:53:06.200
You'll be shot from behind by the guys at his local.

00:53:06.540 --> 00:53:09.360
I'll be sure to watch my back.

00:53:09.360 --> 00:53:10.910
Did you come just to say that?

00:53:11.980 --> 00:53:13.870
Will you join my team?

00:53:16.040 --> 00:53:18.910
It's an independent offensive unit with top priority.

00:53:20.570 --> 00:53:21.300
Oh, excuse me.

00:53:22.610 --> 00:53:23.490
Hello?

00:53:24.370 --> 00:53:25.680
What?!

00:53:25.680 --> 00:53:27.210
I thought it'd be another two weeks!

00:53:27.210 --> 00:53:28.370
No, sorry.

00:53:29.200 --> 00:53:30.850
Got it. I'll be right there.

00:53:31.270 --> 00:53:33.440
This is big! Her water broke!

00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:35.400
Huh?

00:53:35.400 --> 00:53:37.680
We're gonna have a baby!

00:53:37.680 --> 00:53:39.810
Just wait, I'll be right there!

00:53:39.810 --> 00:53:41.360
We'll talk another time.

00:53:41.790 --> 00:53:43.030
I'm coming now!

00:53:46.340 --> 00:53:49.560
Natural, married, and a father?
